## Harness notes

- Each case builds its own root under `/tmp` with `mktemp -d`, copies `measure/doctor.sh` into `<tmp>/measure/`, writes three stub guards into `<tmp>/tests/`, and writes a stub `pnpm` into `<tmp>/bin/`. The stub logs its argv in `<tmp>/pnpm.log`.
- The 127 case and the 127 run of the tool-failure loop use `PATH=<tmp>/bin:/usr/bin:/bin`. Each asserts `pnpm_absent=1` before the run, so no real `pnpm` runs.
- The exit codes are asserted as integers. The counts carry a label: `cases_total`, `cases_failed`, `pnpm_calls`, `codes_checked`, `pnpm_absent`, `record_lines_checked`.
- Part B reads the record through the `track_dir_resolve` helper, which prefers `measure/archive/<id>` over `measure/tracks/<id>`.
- Each case removes its own root. No fixture entered the repository. No production file changed.

## Sanity check of the test

A scratch copy of the test file, a scratch copy of `measure/doctor.sh` that holds the planned behavior of plan task 2.2, and a scratch record in the planned form of plan task 2.3 make all 22 cases pass with exit 0. The scratch root sat outside the repository and was removed. The real `measure/doctor.sh` and the real record did not change.

The scratch record also proves the Part B checks bite. A record with `STEP 2 ... exit 1` fails `record_step_exit_codes`. A record whose VERDICT code differs from the STEP 4 code fails `record_verdict_code_matches_step4`. A record with a changed STEP command text fails `record_step_commands`. A record that names another owner fails `record_owner_line`. A record under `measure/archive/<id>` is still read.

## Scope

- The dirty paths in `git status --short` before the work were unrelated user work of other tracks and generated artifacts. This role did not touch them.
- The two commits hold `tests/orchestrator_doctor_gate.sh` and `measure/tracks/doctor_gate_repair_20261112/plan.md`. No path under `apps/`, `packages/`, or `services/` changed.

## Next

Task 2.2 is `[~]` and waits for the Green role on another model family. The Green check is `bash tests/orchestrator_doctor_gate.sh --part a` with exit 0.

