# Red round log, Phase 2 task 2.5, round 2

Track: `doctor_gate_repair_20261112`
Phase: P2, F421, the gate records the architecture verdict
Task: 2.5 Red, the remediation of the Phase 2 reviews
Role: Measure Mid Red
Model: minimax-cn-coding-plan/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash
Round: 2

## Bases

- `phase_base_sha=e592f824607cc220c02096e0a66d3174d1fe78ec` (resolved)
- `role_base_sha=ad72cee7a36615704ed955f4d4feb03e951ae5b5` (resolved, the amendment commit)

## Commits

- `50db02a6338faf65c891bb2b1f7b7701e8290df8` — `test(measure): pin the real architecture exit path (track_id: doctor_gate_repair_20261112)`. Test file only.
- `68e7ee750dc92f6b0affcf3c2c1e5af56e63dcd0` — `docs(measure): log the doctor task 2.5 red evidence (track_id: doctor_gate_repair_20261112)`. Plan file only.

## Defect of the reviews

The real architecture CLI exits 2 on master. The root script `architecture:check` holds two pnpm layers, and each layer reports 1 for a failed child. The gate read the exit of the wrapper, so it recorded a tool failure as a boundary verdict. The stub of round 1 returned the code of the case directly, so the harness could not see the mapping.

The amendment commit `ad72cee7a` rewrote spec.md FR-3, AC-5, and AC-6, plan.md task 2.5, and test-strategy.md. The Red role of this round follows the amended files.

## Harness change

- The stub of step 4 is now `tsx` at `<tmp>/node_modules/.bin/tsx`. The step 4 command changes into `<tmp>/packages/architecture-enforcement`, so the relative path `../../node_modules/.bin/tsx` resolves the stub. The harness models the real call path with no pnpm layer.
- The stub logs its argv in `<tmp>/tsx.log` and exits with the code of the case. It prints the case message on stderr when the case sets one.
- The harness writes no `pnpm` stub. The `PATH` of every run is `<tmp>/bin:/usr/bin:/bin`, so the real `pnpm` never runs.
- The 127 case and the 127 branch of `tool_failure_codes` assert `tsx_absent=1` before the gate runs. The assertion reads `test -x <tmp>/node_modules/.bin/tsx`. This is the fix of Review A F203.
- Each case removes its own root. No fixture entered the repository. No production file changed.

